1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,378
He repaired lamps in a workshop. The bench stayed

2
00:00:04,378 --> 00:00:08,755
bright long after closing. He felt dimmer every morning.

3
00:00:09,175 --> 00:00:12,794
The extra hours had a reason. A late delivery.

4
00:00:12,794 --> 00:00:16,412
A bill. A customer who needed a lamp for

5
00:00:16,412 --> 00:00:20,031
a shop opening. He could manage one difficult week.

6
00:00:20,451 --> 00:00:23,709
Another week arrived. He erased the end time from

7
00:00:23,709 --> 00:00:26,968
his schedule and wrote a new promise beside it.

8
00:00:26,968 --> 00:00:30,226
The promise always belonged to someone else.

9
00:00:30,646 --> 00:00:34,110
He skipped lunch to finish a repair. When his

10
00:00:34,110 --> 00:00:37,574
hands shook, he held the screwdriver tighter. When he

11
00:00:37,574 --> 00:00:41,037
made a mistake, he stayed later to correct it.

12
00:00:41,457 --> 00:00:44,960
He ate standing beside the sink. The food cooled

13
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:48,462
while he answered messages. He could not remember whether

14
00:00:48,462 --> 00:00:51,964
he had tasted it or simply made it disappear.

15
00:00:52,384 --> 00:00:55,194
Friends stopped asking him to come out, then asked

16
00:00:55,194 --> 00:00:58,004
less often how he was doing. He called that

17
00:00:58,004 --> 00:01:00,813
focus. Some part of him was relieved not to

18
00:01:00,813 --> 00:01:03,623
explain himself.

19
00:01:04,043 --> 00:01:07,785
In bed, he counted unfinished orders. When he finally

20
00:01:07,785 --> 00:01:11,527
slept, the alarm seemed to arrive immediately. He began

21
00:01:11,527 --> 00:01:15,270
the next morning already feeling behind.

22
00:01:15,690 --> 00:01:18,589
On the bench sat a note he had written

23
00:01:18,589 --> 00:01:21,489
months earlier: work harder. The words had once sounded

24
00:01:21,489 --> 00:01:24,388
encouraging. Now they were the only answer he allowed

25
00:01:24,388 --> 00:01:27,288
himself.

26
00:01:27,708 --> 00:01:30,532
He assumed tiredness was a character flaw. Other people

27
00:01:30,532 --> 00:01:33,356
appeared to manage more. He compared their visible output

28
00:01:33,356 --> 00:01:36,180
with the part of his own life that was

29
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:39,005
coming apart.

30
00:01:39,425 --> 00:01:41,836
One afternoon, he connected a wire incorrectly. The lamp

31
00:01:41,836 --> 00:01:44,247
stayed dark. He stared at it for a long

32
00:01:44,247 --> 00:01:46,658
time.

33
00:01:47,078 --> 00:01:50,673
He had spent an hour repeating a ten minute

34
00:01:50,673 --> 00:01:54,268
repair. Adding another hour suddenly seemed less like solving

35
00:01:54,268 --> 00:01:57,863
the problem and more like continuing it.

36
00:01:58,283 --> 00:02:01,914
His evenings had become a closed path: accept another

37
00:02:01,914 --> 00:02:05,545
job, borrow from rest, struggle with the work, then

38
00:02:05,545 --> 00:02:09,176
borrow more time. The diagram described his week, not

39
00:02:09,176 --> 00:02:12,807
a medical diagnosis.

40
00:02:13,227 --> 00:02:16,397
He opened the workshop window. Across the street, a

41
00:02:16,397 --> 00:02:19,566
worker locked a door and left. An ordinary gesture.

42
00:02:19,566 --> 00:02:22,736
He realized he could not remember the last time

43
00:02:22,736 --> 00:02:25,905
leaving had felt ordinary.

44
00:02:26,325 --> 00:02:29,695
When his sister called, he nearly let it ring

45
00:02:29,695 --> 00:02:33,065
out. Instead, he answered. She asked a simple question.

46
00:02:33,065 --> 00:02:36,435
Have you eaten? He could not make a joke

47
00:02:36,435 --> 00:02:39,805
come quickly enough.

48
00:02:40,225 --> 00:02:43,078
They met at a cafe. He tried to explain

49
00:02:43,078 --> 00:02:45,931
the orders first. Then he said what he had

50
00:02:45,931 --> 00:02:48,784
been avoiding: I am exhausted, and I cannot seem

51
00:02:48,784 --> 00:02:51,637
to switch off.

52
00:02:52,057 --> 00:02:54,681
She did not tell him to become tougher. She

53
00:02:54,681 --> 00:02:57,305
asked what was urgent, what was promised, and what

54
00:02:57,305 --> 00:02:59,929
he was afraid would happen if he stopped for

55
00:02:59,929 --> 00:03:02,553
one evening.

56
00:03:02,973 --> 00:03:06,160
Some things were genuinely urgent. Some had become urgent

57
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:09,346
because he had agreed too quickly. Some customers had

58
00:03:09,346 --> 00:03:12,533
never asked for the deadline he had silently imposed

59
00:03:12,533 --> 00:03:15,720
on himself.

60
00:03:16,140 --> 00:03:20,160
He sent two uncomfortable messages about revised collection times.

61
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:24,180
One customer was disappointed. Another said next week was

62
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:28,200
fine. Neither response solved everything, but both were real

63
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:32,220
information.

64
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:35,731
He finished the repair already open on the bench.

65
00:03:35,731 --> 00:03:38,822
Then he unplugged the tools, covered the loose parts,

66
00:03:38,822 --> 00:03:41,914
and wrote down where to resume. Stopping needed a

67
00:03:41,914 --> 00:03:45,005
procedure too.

68
00:03:45,425 --> 00:03:48,400
At six thirty, he locked the workshop. His shoulders

69
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:51,375
stayed tense as he walked away. He kept expecting

70
00:03:51,375 --> 00:03:54,350
the phone to announce that leaving had been a

71
00:03:54,350 --> 00:03:57,325
terrible mistake.

72
00:03:57,745 --> 00:04:00,767
At home, he drank water and ate a meal.

73
00:04:00,767 --> 00:04:03,788
The quiet felt unfamiliar. He reached for work twice.

74
00:04:03,788 --> 00:04:06,810
He put it down twice, without pretending that resting

75
00:04:06,810 --> 00:04:09,831
felt easy.

76
00:04:10,251 --> 00:04:14,175
He did not wake up transformed. One evening could

77
00:04:14,175 --> 00:04:18,099
not repair everything. He was still tired, and that

78
00:04:18,099 --> 00:04:22,024
fact deserved attention rather than another punishment.

79
00:04:22,444 --> 00:04:25,758
He made room for a different pattern: notice the

80
00:04:25,758 --> 00:04:29,073
strain, reduce what could be reduced, and protect recovery.

81
00:04:29,073 --> 00:04:32,387
A set of choices, not a guarantee or a

82
00:04:32,387 --> 00:04:35,702
cure.

83
00:04:36,122 --> 00:04:39,141
He marked an end time again. He left space

84
00:04:39,141 --> 00:04:42,159
between jobs instead of treating every empty square as

85
00:04:42,159 --> 00:04:45,178
a failure. Then he checked whether the plan could

86
00:04:45,178 --> 00:04:48,197
actually pay the bills.

87
00:04:48,617 --> 00:04:52,416
The numbers required changes. He reviewed prices, delivery promises,

88
00:04:52,416 --> 00:04:56,215
and the repairs he accepted. A sustainable workshop could

89
00:04:56,215 --> 00:05:00,015
not depend on pretending his time and body had

90
00:05:00,015 --> 00:05:03,814
no limits.

91
00:05:04,234 --> 00:05:08,193
Some afternoons, he caught himself rushing. He checked his

92
00:05:08,193 --> 00:05:12,152
hands, put the tool down, and took a break

93
00:05:12,152 --> 00:05:16,111
before a small error became an evening of repairs.

94
00:05:16,531 --> 00:05:19,997
The exhaustion did not disappear neatly. When sleep and

95
00:05:19,997 --> 00:05:23,462
concentration kept troubling him, he arranged an appointment with

96
00:05:23,462 --> 00:05:26,928
a qualified professional. He did not need to earn

97
00:05:26,928 --> 00:05:30,393
permission to ask for help.

98
00:05:30,813 --> 00:05:34,079
He also told his sister when the week became

99
00:05:34,079 --> 00:05:37,344
difficult again. Not every conversation ended with a solution.

100
00:05:37,344 --> 00:05:40,609
Being less alone with it still changed how the

101
00:05:40,609 --> 00:05:43,875
evening felt.

102
00:05:44,295 --> 00:05:48,165
A customer brought in a brass lamp. He explained

103
00:05:48,165 --> 00:05:52,034
the realistic waiting time before accepting it. Saying the

104
00:05:52,034 --> 00:05:55,904
limit aloud felt uncomfortable. The customer agreed.

105
00:05:56,324 --> 00:05:59,825
At closing time, the lamp was unfinished. He labeled

106
00:05:59,825 --> 00:06:03,325
the parts and stopped. For once, unfinished work was

107
00:06:03,325 --> 00:06:06,826
evidence of a plan continuing tomorrow, not proof that

108
00:06:06,826 --> 00:06:10,326
he had failed today.

109
00:06:10,746 --> 00:06:13,567
Outside, the sky was still light. He heard a

110
00:06:13,567 --> 00:06:16,389
bus pull away and somebody laughing near the corner.

111
00:06:16,389 --> 00:06:19,210
The city contained things that had nothing to do

112
00:06:19,210 --> 00:06:22,031
with his order book.

113
00:06:22,451 --> 00:06:25,864
Over time, some days became easier. Others were still

114
00:06:25,864 --> 00:06:29,278
hard. He kept changing what did not work, including

115
00:06:29,278 --> 00:06:32,691
promises that sounded reasonable until he tried to live

116
00:06:32,691 --> 00:06:36,104
inside them.

117
00:06:36,524 --> 00:06:39,470
He took down the old note above the bench.

118
00:06:39,470 --> 00:06:42,416
In its place, he wrote something less impressive: check

119
00:06:42,416 --> 00:06:45,362
the load. It reminded him to look at conditions

120
00:06:45,362 --> 00:06:48,308
before blaming himself.

121
00:06:48,728 --> 00:06:51,817
You cannot outwork empty forever. If your effort is

122
00:06:51,817 --> 00:06:54,905
consuming the person making it, that deserves care, support,

123
00:06:54,905 --> 00:06:57,993
and practical change. The workshop can wait while you

124
00:06:57,993 --> 00:07:01,081
notice the light.
